PRACTICE — lesson 01: find files by age
---------------------------------------
/work/site is a small website project. Its files were changed at
different times, from 10 minutes to 6 days ago. Without changing
anything inside /work/site:

1. Create /work/changed.tgz with every regular file in /work/site
   changed in the last 24 hours, but nothing from site/cache.
   One file name has a space in it, and it must be in the archive.
2. Write the files NOT changed for more than 72 hours (3 days) to
   /work/old.txt, one per line, sorted, like ./LICENSE.
   Exactly 72 hours, so be careful with how find rounds days.

Check: sh /practice/check.sh     Answer: /practice/solution.md
[exit 0]

# check PRZED rozwiązaniem (oczekiwane FAIL)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
PASS  /work/site still has its 10 files
FAIL  /work/changed.tgz does not exist yet
FAIL  /work/old.txt does not exist yet

RESULT: FAIL (2 check(s) failed)
[exit 1]

# solution.md
$ cd /work/site && find . -path ./cache -prune -o -type f -mmin -1440 -print0 | tar --null -T - -czf /work/changed.tgz

[exit 0]

# check po CZĘŚCI rozwiązania (oczekiwane FAIL)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
PASS  /work/site still has its 10 files
PASS  changed.tgz has exactly the files from the last 24 hours (cache skipped)
FAIL  /work/old.txt does not exist yet

RESULT: FAIL (1 check(s) failed)
[exit 1]

# solution.md
$ cd /work/site && find . -type f -mmin +4320 | sort > /work/old.txt

[exit 0]

# check PO solution.md (oczekiwane PASS)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
PASS  /work/site still has its 10 files
PASS  changed.tgz has exactly the files from the last 24 hours (cache skipped)
PASS  old.txt lists exactly the files older than 72 hours

RESULT: PASS — well done
[exit 0]

